FUN_1000_0bd1 control-block param: widen undefined2 -> undefined2 * (host-pointer, not truncated).

THE MEMMGR ELEMENT-BUFFER-ALLOC WIDTH BUG (docs/stage1.md frontier, gate step (a)).  When the device
buffer allocator DGROUP:0xcc = FUN_1000_182a is driven (element off-screen buffers), the path is
182a -> 184b -> FUN_1000_0a31 (best-fit alloc) -> FUN_1000_0bd1 (owner-flag search helper) ->
FUN_1000_0d70 (unlink).  0a31 receives the control block as its param_5 (a HOST pointer, e.g.
g_mem+120532 = 0x81b5814) and calls FUN_1000_0bd1(param_5).  But 0bd1's Ghidra signature was
`undefined2 param_1` (16-bit) -> the host pointer was TRUNCATED to its low 16 bits (0x81b5814 ->
0x5814 = 22548), and 0bd1 passed that truncated value straight to FUN_1000_0d70, whose reconstruction
(patch 025) derefs param_1 as the control-block host pointer -> `ctl=(uint8_t*)0x5814` -> WILD DEREF ->
SIGSEGV at FUN_1000_0d70+... (gdb-core-verified: 0d70 param_1=22548, 0bd1 param_1=22548,
0a31 param_5=0x81b5814).

The asm is a near call: the control block lives in BP (a caller-preserved register), 0bd1 does not take
a real parameter -- the C model just threads the ctl host pointer through.  Widening 0bd1's param to
`undefined2 *` stops the truncation; the existing `FUN_1000_0d70((int)(uintptr_t)param_1)` then carries
the full 32-bit host pointer (ILP32: native -m32 and wasm both 32-bit ptrs), matching 0d70's
`ctl=(uint8_t*)(uintptr_t)(unsigned int)param_1`.  0bd1's ONLY caller is 0a31 (`FUN_1000_0bd1(param_5)`,
param_5 already `undefined2 *`), so the call site is unchanged and the fix has zero blast radius beyond
the 0bd1->0d70 unlink.  param_1 is used ONLY as the 0d70 argument (never dereferenced or arithmetic'd in
0bd1), so widening is purely a width correction.

BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows and the default boot: the 0bd1->0d70 branch (a free node whose
owner-flag byte has bit1 set) is not exercised by the boot MEMMGR (default boot rc=0, all 19 flows PASS
unchanged); it is reached only on the deeper element-buffer alloc path driven by the mission cascade.
Validated by a controlled throwaway experiment (resolve 22bf's c0cc -> 182a directly): WITHOUT this fix
the run SIGSEGVs in FUN_1000_0d70 (param_1=22548); WITH it, 0a31->0bd1->0d70 runs clean and 182a
completes the allocation (the crash then advances to the still-seg-0 2595 buffer 0x7a42 -- the remaining
buffer-alloc frontier, step (b)).  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.
